  <diagram id="j4Q8wtPt0XpqFIkN41vn" name="Page-22">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1276" dy="606" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="1000" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="ygOOS0vqk_5Iej4t7KrJ-1" value="PART C — QUESTIONS, ASSUMPTIONS &amp; CONTRADICTIONS" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#1F2937;fontSize=30;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="30" width="1500" height="55" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ygOOS0vqk_5Iej4t7KrJ-2" value="DriveNow database design  |  Draft based on SRS Sections 7.1–7.16 and stakeholder interview notes" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#4B5563;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="58" y="88" width="1480" height="35" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ygOOS0vqk_5Iej4t7KrJ-3" value="1. QUESTIONS" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F3F6FA;strokeColor=#AAB6C5;strokeWidth=1.3;fontColor=#1F2937;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=18;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="145" width="1500" height="48" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ygOOS0vqk_5Iej4t7KrJ-4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-family:Arial;font-size:17px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Section 7.1 — Branches and Staff&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;How should the system preserve the history of branch managers, including the date each manager took over and when the assignment ended?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Section 7.1 — Branches and Staff&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;For branches that operate 24/7, should opening and closing hours be stored as a special flag, or as equal/overnight time values?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Section 7.3 — Fleet, Categories, and Pricing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;When a model has its own price, how should the system decide when to use that price instead of the category daily rate?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;4. Section 7.5 — GPS Tracking&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;If a GPS device is removed from one vehicle and installed in another, should the system keep the previous installation history?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;5. Section 7.7 — Customers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Can the same authorized driver be registered under more than one corporate customer, and how should the system identify that person across accounts?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;6. Section 7.8 — Corporate Contracts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Can a corporate customer have overlapping discounts for the same vehicle category, and if so, which discount should apply?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;7. Section 7.9 — Promotions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Does the maximum number of promo-code uses apply across all customers or separately to each customer?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;8. Section 7.10 — Loyalty Program&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;What is the exact rule for calculating earned points and converting redeemed points into a rental discount?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;9. Sections 7.11–7.12 — Reservations and Rentals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;When a reservation becomes a rental, should its status automatically change to Completed, or should it remain Confirmed with a separate conversion record?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;10. Section 7.12 — Rentals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;For a chain of rental extensions, should each new rental store a direct reference to the rental it extends?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;11. Section 7.13 — Insurance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Can the same insurance package be added more than once to one rental, or can each package appear only once per rental?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 9px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;12. Section 7.16 — Payments&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;What information must be stored on a corporate monthly invoice, and how are payments allocated to that invoice?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#AAB6C5;strokeWidth=1.3;fontColor=#222222;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=16;spacingTop=14;spacingLeft=18;spacingRight=16;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="193" width="1500" height="690" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ygOOS0vqk_5Iej4t7KrJ-5" value="2. ASSUMPTIONS" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F3F6FA;strokeColor=#AAB6C5;strokeWidth=1.3;fontColor=#1F2937;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=18;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="905" width="1500" height="48" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ygOOS0vqk_5Iej4t7KrJ-6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-family:Arial;font-size:16px;line-height:1.28&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Section 7.1 — Branches and Staff&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each employee is assigned to one branch.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Section 7.1 — Branches and Staff&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;An employee may have no supervisor; SupervisorID is therefore optional for senior management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Section 7.1 — Branches and Staff&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Branch-manager assignments are stored with their takeover dates so previous assignments can be retained.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;4. Section 7.1 — Branches and Staff&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;An employee cannot be both a rental agent and a mechanic. Agent commission is limited to 15%, and mechanic certification level is from 1 to 5.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;5. Section 7.2 — Training&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each course attempt is stored separately. AttemptNo is included in the employee-course key so failed attempts are not overwritten.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;6. Section 7.3 — Fleet, Categories, and Pricing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Category rates are kept with effective dates. A model-specific rate is used for models that have their own price.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;7. Section 7.4 — Vehicle Equipment&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The extra charge applied to a rental is stored on the rental-extra record so later price changes do not change old rentals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;8. Section 7.5 — GPS Tracking&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A GPS device may be unassigned while it is in the warehouse; its vehicle reference is optional until installation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;9. Sections 7.6 and 8 — Vehicle Transfers / Interview Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every transfer is recorded with its source branch, destination branch, date/time, odometer reading, and responsible employee. Source and destination branches must be different.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;10. Section 7.7 — Customers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Customer phone numbers are stored separately because every customer has one or more phone numbers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;11. Section 7.7 — Customers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A corporate authorized driver is identified within their company by DriverNo; the driver record depends on that corporate customer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;12. Section 7.8 — Corporate Contracts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Corporate discounts are recorded by customer and category with their validity dates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;13. Section 7.9 — Promotions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A reservation can use zero or one promo code.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;14. Section 7.10 — Loyalty Program and Section 8 — Interview Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every points movement is stored as a separate transaction. The customer tier is calculated from the points balance rather than entered manually.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;15. Sections 7.11–7.12 — Reservations and Rentals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A reservation can produce at most one rental. A rental may also be created without a reservation for a walk-in customer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;16. Section 7.12 — Rentals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Additional drivers are recorded against the rental, and the daily fee charged is saved for that rental.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;17. Section 7.13 — Insurance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The insurance price charged is saved on the rental-package record to preserve the historical price.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;18. Section 7.14 — Damage, Violations, and Feedback&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Damage photos are stored as separate records/links. A rental can have at most one feedback submission.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;19. Section 7.15 — Maintenance and Parts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Mechanic hours are recorded for each job assignment. Parts-used records keep the unit cost at the time of use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;20. Section 7.15 — Maintenance and Parts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Supplier-part records store the supplier price and delivery lead time for each supplied part.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;21. Section 7.16 — Payments and Section 8 — Interview Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment amounts must be greater than zero. A transaction reference is required for card/bank payments and is unique; cash payments have no reference.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;22. Section 7.16 — Payments&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Corporate customers are billed monthly through invoices rather than being required to pay separately for each rental.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#AAB6C5;strokeWidth=1.3;fontColor=#222222;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=16;spacingTop=14;spacingLeft=18;spacingRight=16;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="953" width="1500" height="1030" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ygOOS0vqk_5Iej4t7KrJ-7" value="3. CONTRADICTIONS / POTENTIAL AMBIGUITIES" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F3F6FA;strokeColor=#AAB6C5;strokeWidth=1.3;fontColor=#1F2937;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=18;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="2005" width="1500" height="48" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ygOOS0vqk_5Iej4t7KrJ-8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-family:Arial;font-size:17px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 12px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Potential contradiction / ambiguity&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Section 7.7 — Customers:&lt;/b&gt; Authorized corporate drivers are described as being known only through their company.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Section 8 — Stakeholder Interview Notes (Rana Adel):&lt;/b&gt; Some corporate drivers may also be individual customers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Design note:&lt;/i&gt; This is a possible ambiguity rather than a definite conflict: the same person may have an individual customer record while also having a separate company-specific authorized-driver record.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 12px 0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Potential contradiction / ambiguity&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Section 7.16 — Payments:&lt;/b&gt; A rental may have several payments, such as a deposit, final payment, or later charges.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Section 7.16 — Finance Note:&lt;/b&gt; Corporate clients usually do not pay per rental; they receive one invoice at the end of each month.&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Design note:&lt;/i&gt; These statements describe different payment flows, but the SRS does not fully explain how corporate invoice payments are linked to the rentals included in the invoice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Note:&lt;/b&gt; No definite contradiction has been confirmed; the two items above are potential ambiguities that should be clarified with the stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#AAB6C5;strokeWidth=1.3;fontColor=#222222;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=16;spacingTop=14;spacingLeft=18;spacingRight=16;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="2053" width="1500" height="390" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
